      "reasoning": "All four occurrences explicitly say anhydrous Na2SeO3 inside trace-mineral preparations. The original ATCC1191 formulation lists1 mg in Wolfe's modified mineral elixir, consistent in substance with0.001g in the other trace supplements. CHEBI:48843 has2Na.O3Se and is disodium selenite; CHEBI:131361 pentahydrate is a different supplied form. The existing Na2seo3 owner is the appropriate chemical candidate. Its inherited malformed Na2Se2O3 alias/stock alias obligations remain separate and are not approved by this source-specific match.",
      "applicability": "Individually reviewed source case 9: 'Na2SeO3 (anhydrous)'; all 4 original occurrence IDs and full frozen recipe contexts are retained in RS-009-FROZEN. Primary references are scoped to those exact recipes or explicitly identified chemical/product candidates; no identity or concentration is transferred to a different preparation. This review preserves every inherited source/native hold and does not approve roles or release.",
